                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "89c0f161-911d-4a9c-b272-524fe6d80214",
                        "source_entry_id": "99f63a62-cf2b-38be-982e-9a224cb8dfc7",
                        "source_sense_id": "4acdadbc-6c03-34b3-9b55-7ebf834bf8ac",
                        "target_lang_word": "disgrace",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "disgrace",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "af9f5d1c-214c-3f41-8c98-ba33b4a6b5be",
                                        "entry_id": "418ac08e-bc44-3cce-a52d-3ddaf9064f33",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The condition of being out of favor; loss of favor, regard, or respect."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cbc174b0-9d1e-4575-ac38-d9b3727b12c9",
                                                "sense_id": "af9f5d1c-214c-3f41-8c98-ba33b4a6b5be",
                                                "text": "I heare / Macduffe liues in diſgrace. Sir, can you tell / Where he beſtowes himſelfe?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6be99cd5-8000-39e5-aab9-78c3cfd109e1",
                                        "entry_id": "418ac08e-bc44-3cce-a52d-3ddaf9064f33",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The state of being dishonored, or covered with shame."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7756053a-8f4a-47b8-a6dc-35ce986c9d1f",
                                                "sense_id": "6be99cd5-8000-39e5-aab9-78c3cfd109e1",
                                                "text": "Now she lives in disgrace."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "161ed4fb-fdb4-3973-bd91-75d3def376ac",
                                        "entry_id": "418ac08e-bc44-3cce-a52d-3ddaf9064f33",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Something which brings dishonor; the cause of reproach or shame; great discredit."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6366a8e0-9952-49d6-826e-46e7372d03ac",
                                                "sense_id": "161ed4fb-fdb4-3973-bd91-75d3def376ac",
                                                "text": "His behaviour at the party was a total disgrace! He was leeching on all the ladies, and insulting the men."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c0e8ca50-9b33-4a8d-8471-0825a5e950d1",
                                                "sense_id": "161ed4fb-fdb4-3973-bd91-75d3def376ac",
                                                "text": "Practice and whipping were alike unavailing, and Epps, satisfied of it at last, swore I was a disgrace—that I was not fit to associate with a cotton-picking \"nigger\"—that I could not pick enough in a day to pay the trouble of weighing it, and that I should go into the cotton field no more."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "74fcdf24-767f-3906-890a-83d77428e0ad",
                                        "entry_id": "418ac08e-bc44-3cce-a52d-3ddaf9064f33",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An act of unkindness; a disfavor."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "358e13b3-720c-4406-b42c-04b97bbfb423",
                                                "sense_id": "74fcdf24-767f-3906-890a-83d77428e0ad",
                                                "text": "As for the pulling of them [ambitious men] downe, if the Affaires require it, and that it may not be done with ſafety ſuddainly, the onely Way is, the Enterchange, continually of Fauours, and Diſgraces, whereby they may not know, what to expect; And be, as it were, in a Wood."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "disgrace",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e20ef1d8-7040-3dc1-b0a5-da0a9fb4735f",
                                        "entry_id": "3de008e8-961c-3a15-a0c5-566717b3bb8c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To put someone or something out of favor; to bring shame or ignominy upon."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e07fe5c7-a9db-4a30-a640-26c42383455e",
                                                "sense_id": "e20ef1d8-7040-3dc1-b0a5-da0a9fb4735f",
                                                "text": "[…] some families renounced the use of a certain praenomen which had been disgraced by one of their name […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "80c3ac0b-65a8-40c2-999a-384ef8d0c077",
                        "source_entry_id": "99f63a62-cf2b-38be-982e-9a224cb8dfc7",
                        "source_sense_id": "4acdadbc-6c03-34b3-9b55-7ebf834bf8ac",
                        "target_lang_word": "embarrassment",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "embarrassment",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7d38e310-fde6-3262-9657-1a4eeae66d07",
                                        "entry_id": "3e594cde-ab19-3e19-9f03-dd2687313533",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A state of discomfort arising from bashfulness or consciousness of having violated a social rule; humiliation."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "363f1630-9905-403a-b825-621d028ffa45",
                                                "sense_id": "7d38e310-fde6-3262-9657-1a4eeae66d07",
                                                "text": "The desired effect [of affectionate teasing] is a look of pleasurable embarrassment, as if you administered a compliment. Anyone who doesn't stop teasing immediately upon producing real embarrassment, anger or tears is not really teasing."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c97100a4-9d24-3c2c-8d12-a395506a503f",
                                        "entry_id": "3e594cde-ab19-3e19-9f03-dd2687313533",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person or thing which is the cause of humiliation to another."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b7385b28-2542-4664-9f68-7a453fc6cfdc",
                                                "sense_id": "c97100a4-9d24-3c2c-8d12-a395506a503f",
                                                "text": "Jack, you are an embarrassment to this family."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "73980ff0-ab7a-44c4-b57d-5995b12f82aa",
                                                "sense_id": "c97100a4-9d24-3c2c-8d12-a395506a503f",
                                                "text": "Losing this highly publicized case was an embarrassment to the firm."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ad2ee4a5-0ead-4f48-a68c-4ff89d55a597",
                                                "sense_id": "c97100a4-9d24-3c2c-8d12-a395506a503f",
                                                "text": "The audacious hijacking in Paris of a van carrying the baggage of a Saudi prince to his private jet is obviously an embarrassment to the French capital, whose ultra-high-end boutiques have suffered a spate of heists in recent months."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7088e8af-b87a-3bfe-a6b4-11703bb1a965",
                                        "entry_id": "3e594cde-ab19-3e19-9f03-dd2687313533",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A large collection of good or valuable things, especially one that exceeds requirements or causes some sort of hindrance."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fb3aae4f-0a0e-4a07-add4-0b9d17e0200b",
                                                "sense_id": "7088e8af-b87a-3bfe-a6b4-11703bb1a965",
                                                "text": "There are over 5,000 Americans now in Paris, many artists, singers, musicians, writers, and actors, so many, indeed, the committee could hardly pick a program from an embarrassment of volunteers."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2a045c50-2e31-47b4-be0b-7af9941c1df7",
                                                "sense_id": "7088e8af-b87a-3bfe-a6b4-11703bb1a965",
                                                "text": "The landscape presented an embarrassment of riches for the industrial archaeologist, and eighteenth- and nineteenth-century remains were still visible in abundance"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a24004b6-c961-4f21-9ace-1d8792a5b3a6",
                                                "sense_id": "7088e8af-b87a-3bfe-a6b4-11703bb1a965",
                                                "text": "At one time, I reflected, we'd had an embarrassment of good, qualified squad leader—ready men in the platoon."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fd6f309a-78fd-3576-ae21-66640c3ae422",
                                        "entry_id": "3e594cde-ab19-3e19-9f03-dd2687313533",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A state of confusion; hesitation; uncertainty."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "49e09e1e-72b2-4f27-8567-192e24d7b82e",
                                                "sense_id": "fd6f309a-78fd-3576-ae21-66640c3ae422",
